From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:12:45 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] state: FTS gate keeps the schema memo, detaches under the
 lock, remembers only lasting refusals [daveey]

Second review of the free-path gates (2026-11-19):
- per-thread plan state lives in a module WeakKeyDictionary, not in vars(db): the schema-init memo snapshots
  vars(db) and had stopped memoizing every open (12 memo tests).
- the trash verification plans outside self._lock; its schema read and any detach now take the lock instead of
  writing inside another thread's transaction on the shared connection.
- a memo hit replayed through an attempt plan logs at debug on runtime paths too.
- busy/locked/IO plan failures are not remembered across processes; only a corrupt image or an attributed refusal is.
- optimize_fts returns 0 (no error) when the gate only lost a race (schema moved, no plan); it raises only on a
  refusal or a named family.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
